<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <RootNamespace>Nexus.Intelligence.LiveSmokeHost</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>Nexus.Intelligence.LiveSmokeHost</AssemblyName>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
    <!-- The estate's own analysers apply; this is a host, not a test, so the test SDK is absent. -->
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!-- W7G.2 GATE 9: the AI Head's live provider smoke host.

       This is the AI Head half of the ownership decision that retired
       samples/Nexus.Platform.SmokeHost from Platform. Platform smoke and testing is
       provider-neutral; provider-specific OpenAI / Anthropic / model smoke and E2E testing
       is the AI Head's, and this is where it lives.

       It is a separate console project, and that is a requirement rather than a
       preference: one of the three re-homed assertions is that a real assistant message
       SURVIVES A PROCESS RESTART, and no process can restart itself. The suite launches THIS
       host as a child process to write the message, and launches it a second time to read
       it back.

       Two deliberate differences from the Platform sample it replaces, both of which
       remove a defect rather than carry it across:
         1. It holds no C:\Personal path. The retired sample's StoreSecretResolver
            hardcoded C:\Personal\Nexus.Intelligence\src\Nexus.Intelligence.Api to find a
            user-secrets store; credential custody here is the environment, through the
            estate's own neutral EnvironmentSecretResolver, so there is no path to hardcode.
         2. It composes the AI Head's real composition root (AddNexusIntelligence) and the
            real provider adapter, so what it drives is the estate rather than a
            reimplementation of it. -->

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\src\Nexus.Intelligence.Api\Nexus.Intelligence.Api.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\src\Nexus.Platform.Providers.OpenAI\Nexus.Platform.Providers.OpenAI.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <FrameworkReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.App" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
